{"name":"Real Mccoy","hex":"#00577e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"real","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["True, genuine, not merely nominal or apparent.","Genuine, not artificial, counterfeit, or fake."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Really; very."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/real"}],"entries":[{"title":"Real McCoy (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Real McCoy is a German Eurodance and pop music project best known for their hit singles throughout the mid-1990s: \"Another Night\", \"Automatic Lover \", \"Run Away\", \"Love & Devotion\", \"Come and Get Your Love\", and \"One More Time\". Their first U.S. album Another Night went multi-platinum and charted in countries around the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Ojay2006.jpg/330px-Ojay2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Real_McCoy_(band)"},{"title":"Real McCoy (ferry)","blocks":[{"text":"Real McCoy was a ferryboat that operated for 63 years from Rio Vista, California on the Ryer Island Ferry route as part of California State Route 84, and was the oldest and most reliable piece of equipment owned by the California Department of Transportation. During its operating life – making the trip 24 hours per day, 7 days per week and roughly 200 trips a day – totaling approximately 460,000 safe passages over the 800-foot (240 m) gap in the Sacramento River delta, between Ryer Island and Rio Vista."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/OldRealMcCoyFerry.jpg/330px-OldRealMcCoyFerry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Real_McCoy_(ferry)"},{"title":"The real McCoy","blocks":[{"text":"\"The real McCoy\" is an idiom and metaphor used in much of the English-speaking world to mean \"the real thing\" or \"the genuine article\", e.g. \"he's the real McCoy\". The phrase has been the subject of numerous false etymologies."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_real_McCoy"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Frank_Hassas_and_Juergen_Wind.jpg/330px-Frank_Hassas_and_Juergen_Wind.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Frank_Hassas_and_Juergen_Wind.jpg/330px-Frank_Hassas_and_Juergen_Wind.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Real McCoy producers Frank Hassas (left) and Juergen Wind (right) at Wind Studios B.C in Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFrank_Hassas_and_Juergen_Wind.jpg"}],"sounds":{"real":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9d/En-uk-real.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9d/En-uk-real.ogg/En-uk-real.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/14/En-us-real.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/14/En-us-real.ogg/En-us-real.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5d/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-real_%28Spanish%29.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5d/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-real_%28Spanish%29.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-real_%28Spanish%29.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5d/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-real_%28Spanish%29.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-real_%28Spanish%29.wav.ogg"